cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use QSO in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Metatron QSO: validated quantum simulation in pure Rust"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Klemm
    given-names: Sebastian
repository-code: "https://github.com/LashSesh/qso"
url: "https://github.com/LashSesh/qso"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 1.4.0
date-released: 2026-10-25
keywords:
  - quantum computing
  - quantum simulation
  - quantum walks
  - state transfer
  - QAOA
  - VQE
  - boson sampling
  - error mitigation
  - quantum trajectories
  - quantum chemistry
  - Hamiltonian simulation
  - amplitude estimation
  - Rust
abstract: >-
  Statevector and density-matrix simulation of quantum circuits with exact
  adjoint gradients, variational algorithms (VQE, QAOA, classifiers),
  continuous- and discrete-time quantum walks with exact symmetry
  reduction, state-transfer analysis and walk circuits, graph isomorphism,
  exact boson sampling, device-like noise models with quantum trajectories,
  and error mitigation (readout calibration, zero-noise extrapolation,
  probabilistic error cancellation, Pauli twirling) with classical shadows
  and standard errors on every estimate, Hamiltonian simulation with
  rigorous Trotter error bounds, electronic structure (fermion-to-qubit
  mappings, FCIDUMP integrals, UCCSD, ADAPT-VQE), excited states, quantum
  natural gradient, QUBO/QAOA mixers and amplitude estimation, written in
  pure Rust with Python bindings.
  Every algorithm is validated against closed-form or published results.
